Subject: Port option: keep the original's per-frame steps at higher rates
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509

A few things outside the fixed simulation advance a fixed step per drawn
frame, or decide once per frame, instead of following elapsed time. Above the
original frame rate (previous patch) they would speed up, so each keeps the
original's pace: a continuous step scales with the frame's real length in
original frames, and a discrete change happens only on original frames
(about as many a second as the original drew, 59.94 or 50).

- cCameraManager::Update eases presentation cameras (front-end scripts, the
  Hall of Fame, the trophy room) by g_fSimulationTick per frame.
- Presentation::UpdateAndRenderLetterBox moves the cutscene bars 0.05 per
  frame.
- The skinned multi-light material steps its animated texture with the
  rendered frame count.
- WorldEffect::Update and BasicStadium's cutscene effects roll their emission
  chance on every frame once they are due.
- GLTextureAnim::Update and Blinker::Update drop the leftover time when they
  change image, so each image lasts whole frames of the original rate.
- FEImpostorCharacter::Render rolls its dimmed flicker on every frame.

Everything else that runs per frame was checked and follows elapsed time or
the VI retrace. Without a raised frame rate these hooks take the original
path.

